  "provider_query": "Which organization does the CVE program identify as the source of CVE records used by NVD",
  "answer": "**The MITRE Corporation (via the CVE List / CVE Program it operates).**\n\nThe CVE Program states that the CVE List is the feed NVD uses. NVD (NIST, launched 2005) builds on CVE Records from that list with enrichment such as CVSS, CWE, and CPE. Key points from CVE Program sources:\n\n- CVE and NVD are separate programs. The CVE List, launched by The MITRE Corporation in 1999 as a community effort, “feeds NVD,” which has historically built on the information in CVE Records.  \n- MITRE (through the DHS FFRDC HSSEDI) runs the CVE Program Secretariat, MITRE Top-Level Root, and CNA of Last Resort functions; MITRE owns the CVE trademark.  \n- CVE Records themselves are published by CVE Numbering Authorities (CNAs) and partners into the official CVE List; NVD then consumes published list entries (typically within about an hour) and does not control the underlying descriptions or references.\n\nSources: CVE.org related-efforts and FAQ pages on the CVE–NVD relationship; NVD CVE process documentation noting the program is maintained by MITRE and sponsored by DHS/CISA.",
